<h1>My Neovim setup for competitive programming</h1>
<p>Two configs: daily driver (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/nvim-config">nvim-config</a>) and a lean CP one (<a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/nvim-cp-config">nvim-cp-config</a>). Plus <a href="https://github.com/HimanshuSardana/cpos">cpos</a> to pull Codeforces/CSES problems and run tests without leaving the editor.</p>
<h2>The loop</h2>
<ul><li><code>:CposFetch &lt;url&gt;</code> — scaffolds solution + samples</li><li>One key to compile, run all samples, diff output</li><li>Snippets for DSU, segtree, modint</li></ul>
<h2>Tips</h2>
<ul><li>Keep the CP config plugin-free-ish: startup time matters mid-contest.</li><li>Template with fast I/O baked in.</li><li>Separate leader keys for test vs submit.</li></ul>
</section>
